course: dictionary
lesson: 11369
title: Abdication: giving up the throne
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: An abdication is when a king, queen or other ruler gives up the throne of their own free will. Nobody forces them to go. They choose to step down, and someone else takes over. Look for clues like king, queen or throne to spot the meaning.
explain: «The king's abdication shocked the whole country.» The words king and shocked are clues. A ruler stopped being ruler by choice, and people were surprised. Try your meaning in the sentence: "The king's giving up the throne shocked the whole country." It still makes sense, so you have it.
explain: The word can also be used in a wider, more formal way. «The coach's abdication of responsibility left the team with no plan.» Here it means the coach failed to do the job he should do, as if he had handed it away.
fact: Abdication means giving up a throne by choice.
fact: King Edward VIII abdicated in 1936 to marry Wallis Simpson, and his brother became King George VI.
fact: Queen Beatrix of the Netherlands abdicated in 2013.
fact: In formal speech, «an abdication of responsibility» means failing to do a duty, as if giving it up.
fact: Phrases to know: «the abdication crisis» and «abdication of responsibility».
exercise: «In 1936, King Edward VIII gave up the throne. What is this called?» | Election | Coronation | Inheritance | *Abdication
exercise: «The manager's abdication of responsibility left the team with no plan.» What does abdication of responsibility mean here? | Winning a big prize | Being chosen as a leader | *Failing to do a job you should do | Taking charge of every task
exercise: Which word is the noun for giving up a throne? | monarchy | coronation | jubilee | *abdication
test: «Queen Beatrix of the Netherlands made an abdication in 2013.» What did she do? | She was crowned queen | She died | *She gave up the throne | She won an election
test: Which king gave up the British throne in 1936 to marry Wallis Simpson? | Queen Elizabeth | King George VI | King Henry VIII | *King Edward VIII
exam: Which sentence shows an abdication? | A player leaves the team after a match | A king is crowned at the palace | *A queen gives up her throne of her own free will | A queen rules for fifty years
